# Photograph the game's own Sanctuary indicator on both sides of a melee blow
# struck BY the warded creature. This is the session for bd inc-r1e6.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sanctuary-strike.keys 4
#
# Read the result with tools/check_sanctuary_strike.sh, which is what asserts.
# This file only produces the screens.
#
# WHAT THE BEAD CLAIMS. lib/pspells.irh's Sanctuary registers three TRAP_EVENT
# stati on landing -- EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE), EV_EFFECT and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE -- but
# defines handlers for EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE), EV_STRIKE and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE. The
# two lists do not match. Event dispatch (src/Event.cpp) calls a trap's effect
# only when META(S->Mag) equals the event being thrown, so META(EV_STRIKE) --
# the handler that is supposed to end the spell when the warded creature
# attacks -- is unreachable. The spell's own Desc promises "This protection
# ceases if you take any directly hostile action against another creature".
#
# THE ORACLE IS THE STATUS LINE. src/Term.cpp:185 walks the player's stati on
# every redraw and prints the name of any T_TEFFECT stati whose effect carries
# EF_SHOWNAME. Sanctuary carries it, so the bottom line of the map screen reads
#
#   HP:35/35 Mana:26/26 FP:8/8 GP:68                      Sanctuary |
#
# for exactly as long as the player holds the spell, and stops the moment the
# stati goes. The key script cannot write that word: it only sends keystrokes,
# and the string comes from the player's live stati list, not from a message
# that could linger in the message window.
#
# THREE PHOTOGRAPHS, and the comparison between them is the whole test:
#
#   after-cast       the spell has just landed -- Sanctuary MUST be shown
#   after-nonattack  a summon and three searches later -- MUST still be shown
#   after-strike     one melee blow later -- MUST be gone
#
# THE MIDDLE ONE IS THE CONTROL AND IT IS NOT DECORATION. Without it a build
# that never applied Sanctuary at all, or one that dropped it on any turn that
# passed, would show an absent indicator after the blow and would be read as
# proof that the strike ended it. The searches spend real game time (measured
# on seed 4: turn 198021 at after-cast, 198030 at after-nonattack), so the
# control is a genuine "time passed and nothing hostile happened" case. It is
# also the RAW case: the 3.5 SRD lets the warded creature "use nonattack
# spells or otherwise act" without breaking the spell.
#
# WIZARD MODE SUPPLIES THE SPELL AND THE TARGET, because no scripted walk can
# be relied on to find either.
#
#   * Freeze Monsters (the eleventh row of the Wizard Mode Switches list) stops
#     the goblin acting. A goblin that fought back would attack the player,
#     which is EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE) -- a different handler, and one that rolls a
#     saving throw. This session must measure the player's own blow only.
#   * "Learn Any Spell" takes a typed name and sets SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE
#     (src/Debug.cpp:862). An innate spell costs no mana and casts in 20 ticks,
#     so the character reaches the strike with the spell up whatever god the
#     seed gave the priest. A quoted string in a key script is sent one
#     character per keystroke, which is how "Sanctuary" reaches the ReadLine.
#   * A priest, not the usual barbarian, because the Spell Manager divides by
#     the caster's total mana and a character with none has no business there.
#
# The ESC after chargen-priest.keys answers the "Select direction, location or
# target:" prompt that the last of its four starting-spell keys leaves open.
#
# @choose "Sanctuary" presses the Spell Manager letter beside the spell, which
# casts it outright -- ENTER afterwards would be a second, separate command.
#
# The player-data dump at the end is corroboration, not the oracle: wizard mode
# "Examine Player Data" prints every stati with its event code, so the three
# TRAP EVENT rows tagged (eID:Sanctuary) show which events the spell actually
# trapped. On the unfixed build their Mag values are 2019, 52 and 83 --
# EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE), EV_EFFECT and EV_MAGIC_STRIKE. It is scrolled to with
# DOWN because the dump is longer than the screen.

@include chargen-priest.keys

ESC

# Freeze Monsters, the eleventh row of the switches list.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Sanctuary"
ENTER

m
@choose "Sanctuary"
@dump:after-cast

# What the traps actually are, before anything disturbs them.
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*40
@dump:traps-before
ESC

# --- the control: a summon and three searches, none of them an attack -------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT
ENTER
s
s
s
@dump:after-nonattack

# --- the blow ----------------------------------------------------------------
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:after-strike
v
@dump:strike-log
@while "Messages" ESC

w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*40
@dump:traps-after
ESC
@quit
